    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n[This change](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40645) will create a \"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\" directory instead of using any environment variable. Even if the env. var is set. See the output of the tree command.\n\n> tree\n├── $XDG_CONFIG_HOME\n│   └── nvim\n│       └── nvim-pack-lock.json\n├── init.lua -> ../../dotfiles/.config/nvim/init.lua\n├── lua\n│   ├── config\n│   ├── notes\n│   └── plugins\n├── nvim-pack-lock.json -> ../../dotfiles/.config/nvim/nvim-pack-lock.json\n└── README.md -> ../../dotfiles/.config/nvim/README.md\n\nSystem\n\nOS Garuda Linux\nKernel 7.1.3-zen1-1-zen\nFish 4.8.0\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-941+g7c9222f45e\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n$XDG_CONFIG_HOME is resolved or fallback to `.config`\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev-941+g7c9222f45e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nFish 4.8.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
